  "label": "Puzzle Commercialization",
  "description": "The act of creating and selling puzzles based on historical figures or events is a form of commercialization. While not inherently negative, when applied to figures like Anne Frank — whose story is deeply tied to suffering and loss — it can be seen as exploitative or disrespectful. The meme uses this commercial context to create a jarring contrast with the gravity of her story.",
